<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed 24 civilians in Nigerian villages while bandits in Niger State murdered an immigration officer and burned his body, and similar raids hit Borgu LGA. A Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. The United States blacklisted Nigeria for recruiting child soldiers, and 2,400 recruits, including 800 women, joined Mali's reserve force, while ex-militants in Akwa Ibom pledged support for President Tinubu's re-election. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiVkFVX3lxTE9sSUlMMVRfSEM5VFpsSk1WYkY1RVRJUm1oY3BkRm5udm55MEpaSWl4dFBlTDNFWVVGZTFTSXJsTDVPZ0RqZzVNYXhwTjJ1LThRX3ppT19R?oc=5&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxNX3ZNTW5wZzFMckhvLVJVVkpRU1lCaGNGaTlIU196NUs2V1UxS09NN1lILVdxVmMzQTdmb0V5QWpDY3BHWVBYOHRKcnpmWFVoRWhSUkVzR2VpX19mVFdsYjFCN29XVnpsYjZEajNmSnY2ZzFWNHRia1c3S2tJbU9rbEFubko3NGZKcS02MGc0b2UtM3hUbEpqY1FmUURkNG94UU5uaFVub2NTQ0pnMkNR?oc=5&quot;&gt;streamlinefeed.co.ke&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxNTDJlWmRtTEpEcUY4X2w2SW95dWg3S3lRQkdWand6d3Z1S21IZmJqZEhTclQ3cEpaQ0FXOFpJTGd3bzJlN1F0ZUI0eTdpeWQ2U2NiU1ViVWZFMTdweFZ1c2g5R2FCQzBGMzNkamx2SmFRM0V1VGM0MS1tNGszRnBrUzZyNFZMRzlMZEdUWlFWQjNQUkxVWThfZHRHcEpUZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;beninwebtv.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxQREo3aEY1WkNLZ3RwQWw3Rnh0eUFLZTlzWFdTVEJYSzNNOUJXeGhMdHpmX1FfQ3dLQmZRam45